// Magpie

@100 = ~Magpie~
@101 = ~Magpie~
@102 = ~MAGPIE: Every halfling village has one: the cousin who comes home from the woods with a silver spoon, a lost ring and somebody's spare boots, and swears they just found them. Brandobaris, the halfling god of thieves, luck and adventure, smiles on the Magpie. Treasure has a way of turning up wherever it sleeps, and the dice rarely roll against it.

Advantages:
– +1 Luck and +2 AC (Ducking and Weaving), and again at levels 10 and 20.
– May put 2 slots into Single Weapon Style.
– Magpie's Eye: +15% Pick Pockets, +10% Open Locks and Move Silently, +20% Detect Illusion, and +10 Lore, plus 2 Lore every level afterwards.
– Magpie's Knack: may use arcane scrolls and wands.
– Silver Tongue: 1 use, plus 1 more at levels 6, 11, 16 and every 5 levels after.
  SILVER TONGUE: A creature no higher in level than the Magpie must save vs spell at -2 or stop being hostile.
– Brandobaris's Gift: once a day, when the party rests, a 50% chance that the Magpie finds something: potions, scrolls, gems or ammunition, better as it rises in level, and the occasional wand from level 17.
– Brandobaris's Dice: once a day, when the party rests in a town or a building, the Magpie gambles through the night, winning or losing gold with the odds in its favour.

Disadvantages:
– No backstab, and cannot set traps.
– May only use daggers, short swords, clubs, quarterstaffs, slings, darts and short bows.
– May only wear leather and studded leather armour, and no shields.
– Requires Charisma 15 and Intelligence 9 or higher.
– Must be a neutral good, chaotic good or chaotic neutral halfling.~

@110 = ~Magpie~
@111 = ~Brandobaris's favour: Luck, Ducking and Weaving, and Magpie's Eye.~

@120 = ~Silver Tongue~
@121 = ~Silver Tongue

The Magpie talks its way out of trouble. A creature no higher in level than the Magpie must save vs spell at -2 or calm down and stop being hostile.~

@125 = ~Slip Away~
@126 = ~Slip Away

The Magpie turns invisible, as Improved Invisibility, and is protected by Non-Detection.~

@130 = ~Brandobaris's Favour~
@131 = ~Brandobaris's Favour

Brandobaris's Gift always finds something, and draws from the next tier of treasure up.~
@135 = ~Treasure Hunter~
@136 = ~Treasure Hunter

Each time this ability is chosen, Brandobaris's Gift rolls once more each day.~
@140 = ~Misdirection~
@141 = ~Misdirection

A flick of the wrist and a stolen glance: enemies nearby must save vs spell at -2 or be distracted and harmless for 2 rounds, until something hits them.~
@145 = ~Brandobaris's Grin~
@146 = ~Brandobaris's Grin

Each time this ability is chosen, the Magpie gains 5% resistance to slashing, crushing, piercing, missile and magic damage, and 5% magic resistance.~
@150 = ~Trickster's Turn~
@151 = ~Trickster's Turn

For 1 turn, the Magpie gains +2 to all saves, and enemies nearby get -2 Luck.~
@155 = ~Smooth Talker~
@156 = ~Smooth Talker

+2 uses of Silver Tongue per day.~
@160 = ~Pocket Sand~
@161 = ~Pocket Sand

A handful of sand to the face: one enemy must save vs breath at -2 (-4 from level 30) or be blinded for 2 rounds. Each pick of this ability gives 3 uses a day.~

@165 = ~Brandobaris's Gift~
@166 = ~Brandobaris's Gift

Once a day, when the party rests, there is a 50% chance the Magpie finds something.~
@167 = ~Brandobaris smiles: the Magpie has found something.~
@170 = ~The dice were kind tonight.~
@171 = ~The dice were not kind tonight.~

@180 = ~Magpies cannot use this item.~
